  <title id="memsaccelerometer-title">Schematic of a capacitive MEMS accelerometer</title>
  <desc id="memsaccelerometer-desc">A proof mass m hangs on springs between two anchors and sits between two fixed electrodes, forming capacitances C1 and C2. When the case accelerates to the left, the mass lags behind and moves to the right relative to it by x: the gap to the left electrode widens to d plus x and the gap to the right electrode narrows to d minus x, so C1 falls and C2 rises.</desc>
